Question: mySort() can be written as a wrapper for the betterSort() function. Since mySort() knows the number of elements in the wrapper we can convert it into the start and end indicies. 

void mySort(int array[], unsigned int num_elements) {
    if (num_elements > 0) {
        betterSort(array, 0, num_elements - 1);
    }
}


So what this will do is that mySort() knows the number of elements that need to be ordered. In the betterSort() function we can use num_elements - -1 to know how many elements there are and 0 is the start element. 
